+## Submission
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, server-assigned revision ID, author ID, server receipt time, and base revision ID.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored revision.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original revision unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When two competing revisions for the same visit are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original payloads regardless of the visit's resulting state.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission for a visit that already has accepted revisions omits a base revision ID or names a revision ID not known for that visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When the system accepts a submission, the system SHALL assign a unique revision ID and include it in the acceptance response along with the visit's resulting state.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: If the submitting worker is not authenticated, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: If a submission's visit ID refers to a plot ID not present in the site catalog, the system SHALL reject the submission.
+
+## Visit State
+
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When the system accepts a submission whose base revision ID matches the base revision ID of another accepted revision for the same visit — including when both base revision IDs are null — the system SHALL set the visit to contested state.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: While a visit is in contested state, the system SHALL exclude it from the export-eligible set.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When the system accepts a submission for a visit and the submission names a known revision for that visit as its base, the system SHALL accept the submission regardless of whether that base revision was previously a losing revision in a resolved contest.
+
+## Retrieval
+
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether the visit is in current state or contested state.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a caller retrieves a visit in contested state, the system SHALL include all competing head revisions in the response.
+
+## Resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves a contested visit by naming a winning revision, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity, the winning revision ID, the competing revision IDs, and the resolution timestamp with the resolution record.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator designates a revision as the accepted revision for a contested visit, the system SHALL set the visit to current state with the designated revision as the sole head.
+- [ ] **REC-016**: If a coordinator attempts to resolve a visit that is not in contested state, the system SHALL reject the resolution request.
+- [ ] **REC-017**: If a coordinator names a revision that is not a competing head revision of the contested visit being resolved, the system SHALL reject the resolution request.
